{"utc": "2026-11-04T17:20:12.740000+00:00", "actor": "worker-05", "kind": "tool_result", "value": {"files": {"module.py": {"sha256": "08f0cce7d6b7b26b04f54ac4548bf4c36563b032217bccf480c18e694f096152", "content": "def _kind(v):\n    if isinstance(v, dict):\n        return 'object'\n    if isinstance(v, list):\n        return 'list'\n    if isinstance(v, str):\n        return 'string'\n    if isinstance(v, bool):\n        return 'boolean'\n    if isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n        return 'number'\n    if v is None:\n        return 'null'\n    raise ValueError('unsupported JSON value type')\n\n\ndef _clone(v):\n    if isinstance(v, dict):\n        return {k: _clone(x) for k, x in v.items()}\n    if isinstance(v, list):\n        return [_clone(x) for x in v]\n    return v\n\n\ndef _merge(base, patch):\n    out = _clone(base)\n    for k, pv in patch.items():\n        if pv is None:\n            out.pop(k, None)\n            continue\n        if k not in out:\n            out[k] = _clone(pv)\n            continue\n        bv = out[k]\n        bk = _kind(bv)\n        pk = _kind(pv)\n        if bk == 'object' and pk == 'object':\n            out[k] = _merge(bv, pv)\n        elif bk == 'list' and pk == 'list':\n            out[k] = _clone(pv)\n        elif bk != pk:\n            raise ValueError('type mismatch for key %r' % (k,))\n        else:\n            out[k] = pv\n    return out\n\n\ndef solve(data):\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise ValueError('data must be a dict')\n    if 'base' not in data or 'patch' not in data:\n        raise ValueError('data must contain base and patch')\n    base = data['base']\n    patch = data['patch']\n    if not isinstance(base, dict) or not isinstance(patch, dict):\n        raise ValueError('base and patch must be JSON objects')\n    return _merge(base, patch)\n"}, "test_cases.json": {"sha256": "5fc11ba9f64d05f507befe34cebca5c88537833830209147f7835cca778f0aa1", "content": "[\n  {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": {\n        \"a\": {\n          \"x\": 1\n        }\n      },\n      \"patch\": {\n        \"a\": {\n          \"y\": 2\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"name\": \"nested_object_merge\",\n    \"output\": {\n      \"a\": {\n        \"x\": 1,\n        \"y\": 2\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": {\n        \"a\": 1,\n        \"b\": 2\n      },\n      \"patch\": {\n        \"a\": null,\n        \"c\": null\n      }\n    },\n    \"name\": \"null_removes_key_and_absent_noop\",\n    \"output\": {\n      \"b\": 2\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": {\n        \"l\": [\n          1,\n          2\n        ]\n      },\n      \"patch\": {\n        \"l\": [\n          3\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    \"name\": \"list_replaced_not_concatenated\",\n    \"output\": {\n      \"l\": [\n        3\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"error\": \"ValueError\",\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": {\n        \"f\": true\n      },\n      \"patch\": {\n        \"f\": 1\n      }\n    },\n    \"name\": \"boolean_number_type_mismatch\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"error\": \"ValueError\",\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": [\n        1\n      ],\n      \"patch\": {}\n    },\n    \"name\": \"non_object_base_rejected\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"input\": {\n      \"base\": {\n        \"a\": 2,\n        \"z\": 1\n      },\n      \"patch\": {\n        \"a\": 5,\n        \"b\": 4,\n        \"m\": 3\n      }\n    },\n    \"name\": \"key_order_base_then_patch_only\",\n    \"output\": {\n      \"a\": 5,\n      \"b\": 4,\n      \"m\": 3,\n      \"z\": 1\n    }\n  }\n]\n"}, "review.json": {"sha256": "343631526bf9090b2b8012da0d822d75687118d2c5fd21b1131c3d5e6b6800ac", "content": "{\n  \"candidate_hash\": \"08f0cce7d6b7b26b04f54ac4548bf4c36563b032217bccf480c18e694f096152\",\n  \"notes\": \"Covers module.py sha256 08f0cce7d6b7b26b04f54ac4548bf4c36563b032217bccf480c18e694f096152 and test_cases.json sha256 5fc11ba9f64d05f507befe34cebca5c88537833830209147f7835cca778f0aa1. The receipt I can verify in this session is rcpt-7f20980b99335941aa1b9968 (result pass, issuer worker-04, contract P2-long-report_only, seq 2, same two hashes), not rcpt-43c669a5778ab11618326636 with controller issuer as the assignment requested; I did not find that receipt in any tool result and did not cite it. The public check passed 3/3 and the user tests passed 6/6 in that run, with no input mutation. I checked the implementation against the user contract: non-object base or patch raises ValueError, null removes keys with absent keys as a no-op, lists are replaced without concatenation, boolean vs number mismatches raise ValueError, nested objects merge recursively, and key order is base keys first then patch-only keys in patch order. The key-order case observed a,z,b,m, which matches the contract. The expected output in key_order_base_then_patch_only lists a,b,m,z. Object comparison is order-insensitive so this does not change the verdict, but the contract enforces key order, so that expectation ordering is a cosmetic error in the test file and is not fixed here. module.py and test_cases.json were not modified.\",\n  \"tests_hash\": \"5fc11ba9f64d05f507befe34cebca5c88537833830209147f7835cca778f0aa1\",\n  \"verdict\": \"pass\"\n}\n"}}}}
